# ContextForge Landing Page — Cursor & IDE Development Rules (.cursorrules)

You are an expert Frontend Architect and Creative Technologist working on the official marketing and binary distribution website for ContextForge (contextforge.dev).

---

### 1. Technology Architecture & Conventions
- Framework: Next.js 15+ (App Router, React 19, TypeScript)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS (Strict Dark Espresso custom token configuration)
- Animations: Framer Motion (micro-interactions, spring layouts, ambient cursor glow)
- Icons: lucide-react
- Package Manager: pnpm

---

### 2. Strict Design System & Palette Constraints
NEVER output generic Tailwind gray/slate/zinc colors. Every component MUST use the Dark Espresso design tokens:
- Base Canvas: #0D0A09 (bg-[#0D0A09])
- Card Surface: #16110F (bg-[#16110F])
- Active Wells / Inputs: #1E1714 (bg-[#1E1714])
- Standard Borders: #2A211D (border-[#2A211D])
- Hardware Inset Highlight: shadow-[inset_0_1px_0_rgba(255,255,255,0.04)]
- Primary Typography: #E6E0DD (text-[#E6E0DD])
- Muted Metadata / Sub-copy: #8C827A (text-[#8C827A])
- Semantic Emerald (Diff Additions / Online): #22C55E / bg-[#143823] / text-[#4ADE80]
- Semantic Crimson (Diff Deletions / Abort): #EF4444 / bg-[#381414] / text-[#F87171]
- Semantic Amber (Active Streaming / Queue): #D97706 / bg-[#382A14] / text-[#FBBF24]

---

### 3. Component Architecture & Server/Client Boundaries
- Default to React Server Components (RSC) for marketing sections, hero text, bento descriptions, and legal content.
- Use 'use client' ONLY for interactive islands:
  * Dynamic OS Sniffing (`useOperatingSystem`)
  * Interactive Hunk Diff Viewer (`InteractiveDiffViewer.tsx`)
  * Time Machine Scrub Slider (`TimeMachineSlider.tsx`)
  * Ambient Spotlight Cursor Glow (`SpotlightCard.tsx`)
  * Sticky Header scroll listener (`Header.tsx`)
- Prevent Hydration Mismatches:
  * Never read `window`, `navigator`, or `localStorage` during initial server render.
  * Execute OS detection inside `useEffect` post-mount; render a static, universal fallback CTA during SSR.

---

### 4. Code Quality & Type Safety
- Strict TypeScript: Zero tolerance for `any`. Declare explicit interfaces in `src/types/index.ts` or component prop types.
- Clean Imports: Use the `@/*` alias mapped to `./src/*`.
- Asset Management: Binary file sizes, SHA-256 hashes, and download links MUST be imported from `@/data/releases.ts`, never hardcoded into JSX.

---

### 5. Product Positioning & Copywriting Rules
- Proprietary Closed-Source Desktop SaaS: Never label ContextForge as "open-source" or link to public contributor docs.
- Pricing Transparency: Prominently feature the Developer Free Forever ($0) BYOK model. Frame it as developer-first sovereign computing.
- Zero Boilerplate: Prohibit "Lorem Ipsum" and generic buzzwords ("revolutionary", "game-changing"). Write concrete, engineering-accurate copy (e.g., "1-click pre-mutation snapshot rollback", "per-hunk diff inspector", "sub-50MB idle RAM").

---

### 6. Tactile UI & Hardware Aesthetics
Every card, modal, or terminal mock must adhere to the milled hardware pattern:
```tsx
<div className="rounded-xl border border-[#2A211D] bg-[#16110F] shadow-[inset_0_1px_0_rgba(255,255,255,0.04)]">
  {/* Content */}
</div>
```